{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is used in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated or dead-end obstacles. The design ensures safety by conservative recovery and maximizes coverage by quickly returning to exploration after recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and sensor-driven transitions.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for progress, rotate_clockwise/rotate_counterclockwise for recovery, and full_rotate only as a last resort."
  ],
